----------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications in Fathom relative to upstream x64dbg
----------------------------------------------------------------------
- TraceExport            : export execution traces to JSON / CSV.
- pybridge               : drive the debugger from Python (plugin + client).
- headless templates     : ready-to-use scripts for headless.exe.
- ExtraCmds plugin       : .init / .save / scylla_hide.* convenience commands,
                           a minidump viewer, and the HvKdFusion commands; plus a
                           dockable "HvKdFusion" GUI tab.
- HvKdFusion             : Hyper-V kernel debugging and memory forensics
                           (hvkd*, and "wineye", a native WinDbg-style passive
                           memory REPL with MCP / DAP / gdbserver modes).
- plugin installer       : ScyllaHide / xAnalyzer / PE-sieve / OllyDumpEx, with
                           SHA-256 verification.
- build / release fixes  : minidump viewer CMAKE_SYSTEM_VERSION, unity build.
- branding               : launcher renamed to Fathom.exe with its own icon, the
                           main-window title and the version resource set to
                           "Fathom". The engine executables and DLLs keep their
                           x64dbg names (x64dbg.exe/x32dbg.exe, x64dbg.dll,
                           x64gui.dll, x64bridge.dll) because the plugin SDK and
                           all plugins depend on those names.

